                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3>Finding Your Hospital for Your Condition</h3>
                <table class="condition-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Your Condition</th><th>Recommended Hospital(s) in China</th><th>Why</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>Coronary artery disease / bypass</td><td>Fuwai Hospital, Anzhen Hospital</td><td>Highest cardiac surgery volume in the world</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Heart valve disease</td><td>Fuwai Hospital, Zhongshan Hospital Shanghai</td><td>TAVI/TAVR programs, minimally invasive valves</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Atrial fibrillation / arrhythmia</td><td>Beijing Anzhen, Shanghai Ruijin Hospital</td><td>Ablation volumes and electrophysiology leadership</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Brain tumor / neurosurgery</td><td>Tiantan Hospital, Huashan Hospital</td><td>Largest neurosurgery programs in China</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Spinal surgery / scoliosis</td><td>Beijing Jishuitan, Shanghai Changzheng Hospital</td><td>Spine surgery volume and outcomes</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Hip / knee replacement</td><td>Beijing Jishuitan, Shanghai Sixth People&#x2019;s Hospital</td><td>Joints center experience with international patients</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Lung cancer</td><td>Cancer Hospital CAMS, Shanghai Chest Hospital</td><td>Early screening, VATS, robotic surgery</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Liver cancer / transplant</td><td>Beijing 302, Shanghai Renji Hospital</td><td>Liver transplant leadership, living donor programs</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Colorectal cancer</td><td>Shanghai Cancer Center, Sun Yat-sen Cancer Center</td><td>Multidisciplinary cancer care</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Infertility / IVF</td><td>Shanghai First Maternity, Peking Union Hospital</td><td>Highest IVF volumes and success rates in Asia</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Breast cancer</td><td>Beijing Cancer Hospital, Sun Yat-sen Cancer Center</td><td>Multidisciplinary oncology, oncoplasty</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Gastric cancer</td><td>Peking University Cancer Hospital, Shanghai Ruijin</td><td>Gastric cancer surgical volume</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Eye surgery (cataract/LASIK)</td><td>Tongji Eye Hospital, Shanghai Eye Hospital</td><td>High volume, advanced technology</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Dental implants / cosmetic dentistry</td><td>Stomatological Hospital Chengdu, Shanghai Ninth People&#x2019;s</td><td>High-volume dental centers with international departments</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 4 -->
            <section id="jci-international">
                <h2>4. JCI Accreditation & International Standards</h2>

                <p><strong>JCI (Joint Commission International)</strong> accreditation is the global gold standard for hospital quality and patient safety. For international patients, it serves as the most reliable shorthand for "this hospital meets internationally recognized standards."</p>

                <h3>What JCI Certification Actually Means</h3>
                <p>JCI evaluates hospitals against <strong>1,200+ standards</strong> across patient safety, care quality, facility management, and international patient rights. Hospitals must pass rigorous on-site surveys and are re-evaluated every 3 years.</p>

                <h3>Key Areas JCI Evaluates</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Patient identification</strong> — Correct patient, correct procedure protocols</li>
                    <li><strong>Surgical safety</strong> — Pre-operative checklists, anesthesia standards</li>
                    <li><strong>Medication management</strong> — Safe prescribing, administration, monitoring</li>
                    <li><strong>Infection control</strong> — Hand hygiene, equipment sterilization, isolation protocols</li>
                    <li><strong>Staff qualifications</strong> — Credentials verification, ongoing training</li>
                    <li><strong>Patient rights</strong> — Informed consent, cultural sensitivity, interpreter services</li>
                    <li><strong>Facility safety</strong> — Fire safety, medical gas, emergency preparedness</li>
                </ul>

                <div class="info-box">
                    <h4>&#x1F4A1; China Has 100+ JCI-Accredited Hospitals</h4>
                    <p>China has one of the world's fastest-growing JCI-accredited hospital networks. This means you don't need to sacrifice international-quality standards to access China's cost advantages. Many top specialty hospitals in China hold JCI certification.</p>
                </div>

                <h3>JCI vs. Chinese Hospital Certification</h3>
                <p>China also has its own hospital accreditation system (via the National Health Commission). While this sets minimum standards, it is generally less rigorous than JCI for international patient expectations. <strong>Always ask about JCI status specifically</strong> when evaluating hospitals for international medical tourism.</p>

                <table class="comparison-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Criteria</th><th>JCI-Accredited Hospital</th><th>Non-JCI Hospital</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>International Patient Services</td><td>&#x2705; Dedicated English-speaking coordinators</td><td>&#x26A0; Limited or none</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Medical Records</td><td>&#x2705; International-compatible format</td><td>&#x26A0; May not transfer easily</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Infection Control</td><td>&#x2705; Meets global JCI standards</td><td>&#x26A0; Varies widely</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Insurance Compatibility</td><td>&#x2705; Most international insurers</td><td>&#x26A0; Limited or none</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Continuity of Care</td><td>&#x2705; Records follow international standards</td><td>&#x26A0; May not integrate with home country doctors</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 5 -->
            <section id="checklist">
                <h2>5. Hospital Selection Checklist</h2>

                <p>Before committing to any hospital, use this checklist to evaluate whether it's the right choice for your specific situation:</p>

                <div class="checklist-box">
                    <h3>&#x1F9F9; Your Pre-Booking Hospital Checklist</h3>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">1</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Rankings check:</strong> Is this hospital ranked in the <strong>top 5 nationally</strong> for my specific condition? (Use the Fudan Hospital Rankings or equivalent as your reference.)</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">2</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Volume check:</strong> What is the <strong>annual volume</strong> of this procedure at this hospital? (Ask for a specific number, not a vague claim.)</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">3</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Surgeon check:</strong> Who is my assigned surgeon? How many of <strong>this exact procedure</strong> have they personally performed?</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">4</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>JCI check:</strong> Is this hospital <strong>JCI-accredited</strong>? (Verify on JCI website: <strong>jointcommissioninternational.org</strong>)</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">5</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>International services check:</strong> Does this hospital have a <strong>dedicated international department</strong> with English-speaking coordinators who can guide my entire journey?</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">6</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Cost transparency check:</strong> Can they provide a <strong>written cost estimate</strong> for my complete treatment plan before I travel?</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">7</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Visa letter check:</strong> Can they issue a <strong>medical visa invitation letter</strong> that I can use for my visa application?</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">8</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Second opinion check:</strong> Do they offer <strong>remote second opinions</strong> (telemedicine consultation before I commit to traveling)?</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">9</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Insurance check:</strong> Does this hospital accept my <strong>international health insurance</strong>, or do they work with international insurance providers?</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checklist-item">
                        <span class="check-icon">10</span>
                        <span class="check-text"><strong>Aftercare check:</strong> What is the plan for <strong>follow-up care</strong> when I return home? Will they share records with my home-country doctor?</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h4>&#x26A0; Don't Rely on Hospital Websites Alone</h4>
                    <p>Hospital websites rarely publish updated outcome data and almost never tell you which surgeon is best for your specific case. Use independent coordinators (like our service) that have direct clinical relationships with multiple hospitals — they can match you based on your actual medical profile, not marketing claims.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 6 -->
            <section id="summary">
                <h2>&#x1F4DD; Chapter Summary</h2>

                <div class="info-box success">
                    <h4>&#x2705; Key Takeaways</h4>
                    <ol style="margin: 10px 0 0 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>Match by specialty first</strong> — Choose hospitals based on their ranking for YOUR specific condition, not general reputation</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>Volume drives outcomes</strong> — Higher annual procedure volumes mean better results. China's top hospitals have volume that dwarfs Western hospitals</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>JCI accreditation is your shortcut</strong> — It confirms the hospital meets international quality standards across 1,200+ criteria</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>Ask for specific data</strong> — Volume numbers, mortality rates, infection rates. Vague claims are red flags</li>
                        <li><strong>Use the checklist before booking</strong> — 10 questions that can protect you from the wrong hospital choice</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </section>

            <nav class="chapter-nav">
                <a href="chapter-1-healthcare-system.html">
